    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21856" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">impĕrātīvus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inp-</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj.
		impero, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>proceeding from a
			command</i>, <i>commanded</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">feriae,</span>”
				<i>extraordinary</i>, <i>commanded by a
					magistrate</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Macr. S. 1, 16, § 5 sq.</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">modus,</span>”
				<i>the imperative</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 3, § 313</span></i>
			, and in the grammarians saep.— 
			<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">impĕrātīvē</span></b> , <i>imperatively</i>, Ulp. Reg. tit. 24, 1.</div>
